1><p>A supplement is a factual request to review construction scope, quantities, materials or documented conditions—not a promise that the carrier will approve or pay an item.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">Request a free inspection →</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">Call Majestic</a></div></div></section><section class="resource-body section" id="checklist"><div class="site-shell resource-grid"><aside><span>MAJESTIC</span><strong>SCOPE GUIDE</strong><p>Factual roofing information for homeowners in Charlotte, NC and the surrounding Carolinas.</p></aside><div class="resource-sections"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>Why a scope may differ</h2><ul><li>Roof measurements or waste calculations differ.</li><li>A slope, valley, ridge, flashing detail or related component is absent from the carrier estimate.</li><li>Product availability or manufacturer installation requirements affect the physical work.</li><li>Permit or applicable code requirements must be documented for construction.</li><li>Hidden decking or structural conditions become visible after tear-off and require written change documentation.</li></ul></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>What Majestic prepares</h2><ul><li>A clear description of the construction item under review.</li><li>Roof measurements, quantities and affected locations.</li><li>Photographs and field notes supporting the visible condition.</li><li>Product, manufacturer or code information when relevant to construction.</li><li>An updated written contractor estimate or scope with supporting documents.</li></ul></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>What happens next</h2><ul><li>The homeowner and carrier receive or exchange the requested documents through the authorized process.</li><li>The carrier reviews the information and independently decides whether its estimate or claim decision changes.</li><li>Majestic can answer factual questions about measurements, materials and construction scope.</li><li>Majestic does not interpret policy coverage or guarantee acceptance.</li><li>Any approved or homeowner-authorized construction change is documented in writing before the additional work proceeds.</li></ul></div></article></div></div></section><section class="resource-documents section" id="documents"><div class="site-shell scope-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Majestic documentation</p><h2>What the roofing record may include.</h2><p>The final package depends on what was inspected, what work was authorized and what the carrier or homeowner requested.</p></div><ul><li>Inspection photos and field notes</li><li>Roof measurement report</li><li>Written estimate and scope</li><li>Line-item construction clarification</li><li>Product or code support when applicable</li><li>Revised project documents and written change conditions</li></ul></div></section><section class="resource-callout"><div class="site-shell"><strong>!</strong><p>Majestic has documented supplement experience on roofing projects involving State Farm, Allstate, Liberty Mutual and other carriers. Carrier names do not imply affiliation or endorsement.</p></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">Next step</p><h2>Start with a free roof inspection.</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">Open the roof request form →</a></div></section><footer class="claim-footer"><div class="site-shell"><a href="/" class="brand brand-footer"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span><strong>MAJESTIC</strong><small>ROOFING, INC.</small></span></a><p>Roof documentation is not public-adjuster, policy or legal advice.</p><a href="tel:+19808005991">(980) 800-5991</a></div></footer></main>
